{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Moses called for all the elders of Israel.</b> And they shall say to the assembly:" "<b>And take for yourselves sheep.</b> On the tenth of the month, as HaShem commanded him." "The grammarian said that ושחטו הפסח is from the dagesh conjugation [pi'el], and he did not speak correctly, for ושחטו אותו כל קהל עדת ישראל (Exodus 12:6) is from the light conjugation [qal], and the shin is kamatz according to the rule because of the hidden nun [i.e., the passive/reflexive object marker], only ושחטו הפסח is imperative language from the light conjugation, and we do not find this form in all of Scripture from the dagesh conjugation, and the shin ought to have a chirik under it like משכו, but because of the guttural letter that follows it, the shin is opened according to their rule to do so, like בַחֲרו לכם (Joshua 24:15) and many like this. Therefore the shin will be a kamatz gadol in the imperative, and both are from one conjugation."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:41.961655634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}